{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
You [G]ought to see my Cindy,
She lives a-way down [D]south,
And [G]she's so sweet the honey bees
Swarm [D]round her pretty [G]mouth.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Get a[G]long home, Cindy, Cindy,
Get a[C]long home, Cindy, Cindy,
Get a[G]long home, Cindy, Cindy,
I'll [D]marry you some [G]day.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
The [G]first time I seen Cindy
She was standing in the [D]door,
Her [G]shoes and stockings in her hand,
Her [D]feet all over the [G]floor.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
I [G]wish I was an apple
A-hanging on a [D]tree,
And [G]every time my Cindy passed
She'd [D]take a bite of [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
